// Age of Empires III verisi: scripts/aoe-wiki-data.ps1 -Game AOE3 ile Age of Empires Wiki'den (CC BY-SA) oluşturulur, elle düzenlenmez.
const AOEW = {"game":"Age of Empires III","civs":[{"id":"aztecsageofempiresiii","name":"Aztecs","page":"Aztecs (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Aztecs are one of the three playable Native American civilizations featured in Age of Empires III: The WarChiefs. They are based on the Aztec city states during the last stages of their rule, starting with the reign of Cuauhtémoc in 1520.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"America"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Tenochtitlan"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Cuauhtemoc"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 3 Cords of Wood (300 wood), five Villagers, a Warrior Priest, and an Eagle Scout; all Trading Post sites visible.","War Chief aura doubles the experience from nearby friendly units\u0027 kills.","Warrior Priests can work at the Community Plaza and are counted as two units.","Build the Community Plaza and task Villagers on it to perform powerful ceremonies.","Choose Tribal Council members to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Native American units","items":["Aztec Villager: Villager that gathers resources.","Native Scout: A Native American scout. Good for exploration, but has a weak attack.","Warrior: Quick-training Native defender who quickly loses hit points, becoming less effective over time.","Pistolero: A dangerous outlaw with a pistol.","Comanchero: A dangerous outlaw on horseback.","Renegado: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle.","Captured Mortar: Artillery captured and operated by Native Americans. Fires an exploding shell at buildings or ships.","Native Fishing Boat: Gathers food from Fish or coin from Whales.","Canoe: Native boat that can attack or transport units.","War Canoe: Strong in naval combat when built in number."]},{"title":"Shared Native American buildings","items":["Farm: Slow, infinite source of Food. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Community Plaza: Task Villagers on the Community Plaza to perform a poweful ceremony.","War Hut: Trains and upgrades infantry units as well as defends an area with a ranged attack."]},{"title":"Unique Aztec units","items":["Aztec War Chief: The leader of your Tribe. Possesses many powerful bonuses and abilities. Explores, fights, builds Town Centers and Trading Posts.","Eagle Scout: Aztec scout that flings javelins from an atlatl. Helps the War Chief to explore the map and defeat treasure guardians.","Otontin Slinger: Slinger. Good against heavy infantry.","Puma Spearman: Warrior armed with a deadly spear. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Warrior Priest: Heals injured units and are also effective in combat. Warrior Priests are extremely effective when occupying the Community Plaza.","Arrow Knight: Long-ranged noble that fires flaming arrows. Good against artillery and buildings.","Jaguar Prowl Knight: Stealthy noble armed with an obsidian sword. Good against cavalry and heavy infantry.","Skull Knight: Aztec elite berserker.","Coyote Runner: Fast armored warrior. Good against skirmishers and artillery.","Eagle Runner Knight: Nobleman that flings javelins from an atlatl. Good against cavalry and Hand Shock Infantry.","Tlaloc Canoe: Strong in naval combat when built in numbers."]},{"title":"Unique Aztec buildings","items":["Nobles\u0027 Hut: A powerful temple that provides an excellent defense and trains elite Aztec units."]},{"title":"Unique Aztec ceremonies","items":["Healing Ceremony: Units regenerate hit points while idle.","Garland War Ceremony: Spawns Skull Knights."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/b/bc/Flag_AztecDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"british","name":"British","page":"British","intro":"The British are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III and its expansions The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties. The British are the people hailing from the British Isles in Western Europe and a united kingdom comprising of the English, Scottish, Welsh, and Irish nations.\nIn the New World, the British were one of the most powerful colonizers after defeating multiple European powers. They eventually established thirteen colonies, which later revolted against the British to form the United States of America.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Manors spawn free Settlers"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Longbowman\nRanger\nRocket"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Manor House"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Musketeer (Redcoat)\nHussar (King\u0027s Life Guard)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"London"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Queen Elizabeth"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Canada\nHaiti\nSouth Africa\nUSR"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 2 Crates of Food and 1 Tiny Crate of Food (250 food), 2 Cords of Wood and 1 Tiny Crate of Wood (250 wood), and six Settlers.","The Explorer has +2 Line of Sight and +1 ranged attack range.","Manor House spawns a Settler when built.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Musketeer (Redcoat), Hussar (King\u0027s Life Guard)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Longbowman: Archaic long-ranged archer. Good against infantry.","Ranger: British skirmisher. Equipped with a rifle to counter Heavy Infantry more effectively, but has less range.","Rocket: Heavy artillery that fires a rocket and is good against infantry or buildings."]},{"title":"Unique building","items":["Manor House: More expensive than a normal House. Spawns a Settler when built. Supports 10 population."]},{"title":"Allies, mercenaries and native warriors","items":["Mercenaries trainable in the Tavern with The Mercenary Contractor: Harquebusier, Jaeger.","Mercenaries shippable from the Home City: Irish Brigadier, Swiss Pikeman, Highlander, Harquebusier, Jaeger, Giant Grenadier, Zouave, Elmetto, Li\u0027l Bombard, Jat Lancer, Privateer.","Native warriors shippable from the Home City: Totenkopf Hussar, Drummer, Akan Ankobia, Cherokee Rifleman."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Adventurer, The Bishop, The Mercenary Contractor, The Mohawk Statesman (Fortress Age)","The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Logistician, The Tycoon, The Viceroy (Industrial Age)","The Black Duke, El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["George Washington and Toussaint L\u0027Ouverture (The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Canada, Haiti, South Africa, United States (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/6/64/Flag_BritishDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"chineseageofempiresiii","name":"Chinese","page":"Chinese (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Chinese are one of the three playable civilizations featured in Age of Empires III: The Asian Dynasties based on the Great Qing Empire (大清帝國) during the reign of Kangxi (康熙) in the early modern era. They are widely considered to be an offensive civilization and similar to the Russians in employing lots of cheaper and comparatively weaker units. Unlike the Russians, the Chinese have access to a wide variety of units, and can diversify their army composition thanks to their banner armies providing a set of two types of units.\nThe Chinese in-game have many similarities to their precursor and successor from Age of Empires II and Age of Empires IV, being a \"jack-of-all trades\" civilization with a diverse army, while being a difficult civilization to pick up (in the case of the Chinese in Age of Empires III, they are considered a difficult civilization due to the banner army mechanic making it hard to focus on specific units for their army composition, in addition to the age advancement mechanic with Wonders). Unlike their depictions in the precursor and successor games, in this game the Chinese put more emphasis on rush strategies, but are considered to be a jack-of-all trades civilization due to their ability to diversify their army composition and adapt to different rush strategies. Since the Chinese in Age of Empires III are based off the Great Qing Empire, they are the successors of the Jurchens (Manchu people) from Age of Empires II and Jin Dynasty from Age of Empires IV, instead of the Han Chinese.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Asia"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Beijing"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Kangxi Emperor"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 2 Crates of Food (200 food), 3 Cords of Wood (300 wood), 100 export, six Villagers, a Goat, and a Disciple.","Has a population limit of 220.","Train units in blocks as banner armies.","Villagers gather export as they gather resources.","Build the Consulate to ally with a European civilization and get their units and technologies by spending export.","Build Wonders to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Asian units","items":["Chinese Sentry: Quick-training, Pikeman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Chinese Irregular: Quick-training, musketeer who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time."]},{"title":"Shared Asian buildings","items":["Rice Paddy: Slow, infinite source of Food or Coin. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Monastery: Trains repentant outlaws and mercenaries. Provides Monk improvements.","Chinese Castle: A powerful defensive building that can also train and upgrade artillery.","Consulate: Spend Export here to enter into relations with European powers and gain a powerful bonus. Also use Export to purchase European troops and technologies."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Shaolin Master: Religious leader who trains Disciples, stuns Guardians, and has a chance to inflict a Critical Strike in combat. Explores, fights, and builds Town Centers and Trading Posts.","Asian Villager: Villager that gathers resources.","Chu Ko Nu: Archaic Chinese crossbow that fires at an extremely fast rate. Good against infantry.","Qiang Pikeman: Foot warrior armed with a pike. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Flamethrower: Chinese siege weapon that shoots fire at a short range. Better against infantry than buildings.","Changdao Swordsman: Soldier armed with a very large sword. Good against cavalry.","Arquebusier: Chinese foot soldier armed with a rifle. Good against infantry.","Disciple: Disciple to the Chinese Monk. Good against skirmishers, mercenaries and artillery.","Steppe Rider: Fast cavalry good at raiding villagers or buildings.","Keshik: Mongolian ranged cavalry. Good against cavalry.","Iron Flail: Chinese heavy cavalry. Good against archers, skirmishers, and artillery.","Meteor Hammer: Heavy cavalry that does hand damage from range. Good against archers, skirmishers, and artillery.","Hand Mortar: Weak light artillery. En masse, good against other artillery.","Flying Crow: Heavy artillery that fires a rocket and is good against infantry or buildings.","Fire Junk: Fire Junk. Rams anything on the water and explodes.","War Junk: War Junk. Good at exploring, fishing or transport.","Fuchuan: Fuchuan. A heavy warship that can train units."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Village: Supports 20 population, which can be increased here with improvements. Also fattens livestock faster and trains Goats.","War Academy: Chinese combination of Barracks and Stable. Trains infantry and cavalry in mixed groups. Also, upgrades infantry and cavalry."]},{"title":"Wonders","items":["Confucian Academy: Generates Flying Crow artillery automatically.","Porcelain Tower: Generates resources automatically. Configure it to produce different things.","Summer Palace: Generates Banner Armies automatically. Configure it to produce different things.","Temple of Heaven: Casts the Transcendence ability to heal your units.","White Pagoda: Increases attack and hitpoints of Shaolin Master and Disciple."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/1/1c/Flag_ChineseDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"danesageofempiresiii","name":"Danes","page":"Danes (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Danes are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - The Baltic Powers. They represent the .\nThe kingdom had several colonies across four continents: Africa, Asia, Europe and North America, notable ones include the Danish Gold Coast, both Danish West and East India companies, and Greenland.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Snaphane\nMounted Friskytte\nEspingol\nGunboat"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Customs House\nWatch House\nRound Church"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"All military land units"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Copenhagen"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"King Christian"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"None"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 3 Crates of Food (300 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), five Settlers, and a Customs Wagon.","Age-ups are 20% cheaper but cannot revolt.","Start with a Customs House that holds all resource crates and grants income for shipments of other players, but Home City shipments require +5% xp to be earned.","Watch House replaces House.","Round Church replaces Church."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Crossbowman (Royal Crossbowmen)","Pikeman (Royal Pikemen)","Halberdier (Drabant Halberdiers)","Musketeer (Royal Guards)","Skirmisher (Ski Troopers)","Snaphane (Friskytter)","Hussar (Horse Guards)","Dragoon (Jutland Dragoons)","Grenadier (Royal Grenadiers)","Falconet (Danish Field Guns)","Culverin (Holstein Culverins)","Mortar (Royal Mortars)","Horse Artillery (Norwegian Artillery)"]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Snaphane: Stealthy Danish Militiaman who becomes less effective over time by losing hitpoints. Good for ambushes, especially against Outlaws and Artillery.","Mounted Friskytte: Danish ranged cavalryman. Good against Artillery, Outlaws and Pets.","Espingol: Artillery that fires multiple projectiles. Better against infantry than buildings.","Gunboat: Gunboat. Quickly assembled war boat that is good against warships but loses hitpoints over time."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Customs House: Ships resource crates and creates coin income each time another player receives a shipment.","Watch House: Supports 10 population and has an increased line-of-sight. Trains and upgrades Snaphaner.","Round Church: Defensive Church with a ranged attack. Trickles XP, trains healers and Spies. Good against Mercenaries and Outlaws."]},{"title":"Unique technologies","items":["Disruption","Zealand Jaegers","Royal Service"]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["Commerce Age: The Governor, The Quartermaster, The Inventor, The Naturalist, The Logistician","Fortress Age: The Adventurer, The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Bishop, The Scout, The Marksman","Industrial Age: The Engineer, The Tycoon, The Logistician, The Viceroy, The Cavalry Marshal","Imperial Age: El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist"]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/3/36/AoE3DE_Flag_Danes.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"dutch","name":"Dutch","page":"Dutch","intro":"The Dutch are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. They can be considered the successor state of Burgundy, which ruled over a large part of the Netherlands at its peak.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Settlers replaced by Merchants which cost coin, gather from mines 15% faster, and have a lower train limit\nBanks automatically produce coin"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Merchant\nEnvoy\nRuyter\nFluyt"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Bank"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Halberdier (Stadswacht)\nRuyter (Carabineer)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Amsterdam"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Maurice of Nassau"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Brazil\nIndonesia\nSouth Africa\nUSR"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), 4 Chests of Coin (400 coin), six Merchants, and an Envoy.","The Explorer can train Envoys.","Trains Merchants instead of Settlers, which cost coin instead of food and have a lower train limit (50), but gather from mines 15% faster.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Halberdier (Stadswacht), Ruyter (Carabineer)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Merchant: Dutch villager that costs coin but also gathers coin faster than a Settler.","Envoy: Dutch reconnaissance unit with a good line of sight that benefits from villager upgrades.","Ruyter: Ranged cavalry armed with pistols. Good against cavalry and artillery.","Fluyt: Slow, powerful ship resistant to building fire that can train units."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Bank: Dutch building that produces Coin."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Bishop, The Exiled Prince, The Mercenary Contractor, The Sergeant at Arms (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Logistician, The Tycoon, The Viceroy (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["George Washington and José Bonifácio de Andrada e Silva (The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Brazil, Indonesia, South Africa, USR (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/9/97/Flag_DutchDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"ethiopiansageofempiresiii","name":"Ethiopians","page":"Ethiopians (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Ethiopians are an African civilization introduced in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - The African Royals, based on the early modern Ethiopian princedoms and duchies during the \"Zemene Mesafint\" period (The Era of the Princes), and the empire under reign of Tewodros II (pre-regnal name Kassa Hailu) and his successors, located in eastern Africa, in the lands west of Somalia and south of Egypt.\nThey are also featured in The African Kingdoms with the same name.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Africa"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique building"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Gondar"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Emperor Tewodros"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with five Villagers, a Livestock Market Builder, a Zebu Cattle with 400 food (which start gathering automatically), and 3 additional Zebu Cattle with 135 food each; all Trading Post sites visible.","Gets a free Mountain Monastery Builder with every Age-up.","Can trade livestock in the Livestock Market for wood and coin.","Mountain Monasteries can gather coin and influence when built atop mines.","Choose Alliances to advance in Age.","Minor civilization units, technologies, and Mercenaries\u0027 costs are replaced by influence. Native warriors and artillery are upgraded automatically for free in every Age up."]},{"title":"Shared African units","items":["Ethiopian Villager: Villager that constructs buildings and gathers resources.","Levied Spearman: Quick-training, Spearman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Levied Bowman: Quick-training foot archer who loses hitpoints over time, but gains attack speed at lower health.","Levied Gunner: Musketeer who loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Desert Warrior: Hardy javelin warrior equipped with a large shield. The shield grants different armor types when switching combat stances. Good against cavalry.","Desert Archer: Secretive, skilled archer that can hit distant targets as well as shoot fast at short range. Good against infantry.","Desert Raider: Plundering Desert Raider. Good against buildings.","Javelin Rider: Ranged cavalry. Good against hand cavalry, particularly in melee.","Ethiopian Fishing Canoe: Gathers Food from Fish or Coin from Whales.","Battle Canoe: Battle Canoe. Powerful, agile warship that can also train units.","Cannon Boat: Cannon Boat. Somewhat expensive, but powerful boat good at blasting ships and builders from a distance."]},{"title":"Shared African buildings","items":["Hut: Supports 10 population.","Livestock Market: Livestock Market. Combines Market and Livestock Pen. Can fatten and sell Livestock for wood or gold.","Field: Slow, infinite source of Food or Coin for up to three gatherers. Builds slowly, but is inexpensive.","Port: Builds and upgrades Fishing Boats and warships. Repairs nearby ships.","Watch Tower: Watch Tower that can be used to defend the border.","War Camp: Trains and upgrades African regular units.","Granary: Improves nearby Food gather rates and lures hunt. Builds slowly but for free. Contains hunting and farming upgrades.","Palace: Powerful, defensive building that can also train units."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Ras: Royal Ethiopian hero with a fealty aura. Explores, fights, builds Palaces, Mountain Monasteries, and Trading Posts. Good against infantry.","Zebu Cattle: Herd animal. Fattens over time. Fattens faster if tasked on a Livestock Pen, Farm, or Village.","Abun: Heals injured units from range and during battle. May be tasked to gather at a Mountain Monastery.","Gascenya: Heavy ranged infantry. Good against cavalry in melee.","Neftenya: Skirmisher with high hitpoints. Good against heavy infantry and light ranged cavalry.","Shotel Warrior: Fast moving shock troops that attacks quickly with two curved swords. Good against light infantry.","Oromo Warrior: Powerful heavy hand cavalry with strong ranged and hand attacks. Attacks faster when closer to the enemy. Good against light infantry.","Sebastopol Mortar: Gargantuan mortar which annihilates units and buildings. Slow and expensive.","War Dhow: Powerful, heavy Mercenary Warship with very high hitpoints."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Mountain Monastery: Can be placed on a mine and toggle between Coin and Influence generation. Trains Abun and researches Alliance technologies."]},{"title":"Alliance units","items":["Somalis","Somali Darood Militia","Somali Issa Warrior","Jesuits","Conquistador","Portuguese","Cannoneer","Caravel","Sudanese","Sudanese Dervish","Indians","Howdah","Mahout Lancer","Arabs","Gatling Camel","Mameluke"]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/8/89/Flag_Ethiopian_aoe3de.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"frenchageofempiresiii","name":"French","page":"French (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The French are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III.\nTheir ancestors, the Franks, are featured in Age of Empires II: The Age of Kings, and reappear as French in Age of Empires IV. They held large areas in the New World until the late 1700s, and still have small colonies in South America today.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Train Coureurs des Bois instead of Settlers\nStart with a Native Scout"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Coureur des Bois\nCuirassier"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Skirmisher (Voltigeur)\nCuirassier (Gendarme)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Paris"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Napoleon Bonaparte"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Canada\nHaiti\nRevolutionary France\nUSR"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 3 Crates of Food* (300 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), five Coureurs des Bois, and a Native Scout.","The Explorer builds Trading Posts 33% faster and has +1 ranged attack damage.","Trains Coureurs des Bois instead of Settlers.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Skirmisher (Voltigeur), Cuirassier (Gendarme)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Coureur des Bois: Expensive but powerful villager who gathers fast.","Cuirassier: Heavy cavalry with a trample attack."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Bishop, The Exiled Prince, The Gentleman Pirate, The Marksman, The Mercenary Contractor (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Papal Guard, The Tycoon (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Francisco de Paula Santander and Toussaint L\u0027Ouverture (The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Canada, Haiti, Revolutionary France (exclusive) and USR (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/6/6a/Flag_FrenchDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"germans","name":"Germans","page":"Germans","intro":"The Germans are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. They are primarily based on the Kingdom of Prussia (16th to early 20th centuries) and Holy Roman Empire after the 15th century (1400s to 1806 AD, since Definitive Edition).\nThey are the descendants of the Teutons (featured in Age of Empires II) and a continuation of the Holy Roman Empire (featured in Age of Empires IV) who inhabited regions in modern-day Germany.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Receive Uhlans with Home City shipments"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Settler Wagon\nLandwehr\nDoppelsoldner\nUhlan\nWar Wagon"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Mercenary Camp"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Skirmisher (Needle Gunner)\nUhlan (Prussian Uhlan)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Berlin"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Frederick the Great"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Argentina\nHungary\nLivonia\nPrussia\nGerman Confederation (via Prussia only)"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 3 Crates of Food (300 food), 1 Cords of Wood (100 wood), 1 Chests of Coin (100 coin), and three Settler Wagons.","The Explorer has +15% regeneration.","Receive Uhlans with every Home City shipments (except TEAM) from Commerce Age and beyond (mercenary shipments contain more units instead), but Home City shipments require +10% xp to be earned (this debuff will not be removed after revolting, and the player will not be able to receive Uhlans from Home City shipments either. If the player chooses The Logistician to age up and then revolt into Argentina, Exploration Age shipments that the Germans already have before the revolt will still ship 1 Uhlan).","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Skirmisher (Needle Gunner), Uhlan (Prussian Uhlan)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Settler Wagon: A German villager that is more expensive but gathers faster than a Settler.","Landwehr: Affordable German ranged infantry armed with a rifle. Inflicts higher base damage at the expense of less bonus damage.","Doppelsoldner: Heavy swordsman with a sweep attack.","Uhlan: Hand cavalry that sacrifices hitpoints for attack.","War Wagon: Hussite horse-drawn wagon outfitted with cannon."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Mercenary Camp: Trains sinister outlaws and mercenaries."]},{"title":"Allies, mercenaries and natives","items":["Mercenaries trainable in the Mercenary Camp: Landsknecht, Jaeger, Giant Grenadier, Black Rider, Pandour.","Mercenaries shippable from the Home City: Landsknecht, Jaeger, Giant Grenadier, Black Rider, Pandour, Bosniaks, Harquebusiers, Elmetti, Highland Army, Holy Roman Army.","European natives trainable in the Native Embassy through the Prince Electors card: Mounted Infantry, Line Infantry, Totenkopf Hussar, Black Brunswicker, Drummer, Royal Huntsman, Northern Musketeer, Trabant, Saxon Cuirassier, Mountain Trooper, Chevauleger.","European natives shippable from the Home City: Trabant, Saxon Cuirassier, Mounted Infantry, Line Infantry."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Bishop, The Exiled Prince, The Gentleman Pirate, The Marksman, The Sergeant at Arms (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The Papal Guard, The Tycoon, The Viceroy (Industrial Age)","The Black Duke, El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["José de San Martín and Simón Bolívar (in The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Argentina, Hungary, Livonia, Prussia, German Confederation (via Prussia only)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/d/da/Flag_GermanDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"haudenosaunee","name":"Haudenosaunee","page":"Haudenosaunee","intro":"The Haudenosaunee (known as the Iroquois before the Definitive Edition) is a civilization in Age of Empires III: The WarChiefs, based on the Native American confederacy that thrived in the northeastern part of North America.\nThe Haudenosaunee first appeared as a minor civilization in Age of Empires III, before being reintroduced as a playable civilization.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"North America"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Caughnawaga"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Hiawatha"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 5 Crates of Food (500 food), 1 Cords of Wood (100 wood), five Villagers, and a Travois; all Trading Post sites visible.","War Chief aura increases the hit points of nearby friendly units.","[[Villager (tag).","Travois build most buildings for free.","Cannot gather coin by mining; build a Tribal Marketplace next to a mine and assign Villagers on it to gather coin from the mine instead.","Build the Community Plaza and task Villagers on it to perform powerful ceremonies.","Choose Tribal Council members to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Native American units","items":["Native Villager: Villager that gathers resources.","Haudenosaunee Healer: Heals injured units.","Native Scout: A Native American scout. Good for exploration, but has a weak attack.","Warrior: Quick-training Native defender who quickly loses hit points, becoming less effective over time.","Pistolero: A dangerous outlaw with a pistol.","Comanchero: A dangerous outlaw on horseback.","Renegado: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle.","Captured Mortar: Artillery captured and operated by Native Americans. Fires an exploding shell at buildings or ships.","Native Fishing Boat: Gathers food from Fish or coin from Whales.","Canoe: Native boat that can attack or transport units.","War Canoe: Strong in naval combat when built in number."]},{"title":"Shared Native American buildings","items":["Tribal Marketplace: Source of Coin that lasts longer. Must be built next to a Mine. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Farm: Slow, infinite source of Food. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Community Plaza: Task Villagers on the Community Plaza to perform a powerful ceremony.","War Hut: Trains and upgrades infantry units as well as defends an area with a ranged attack.","Corral: Trains and upgrades hand and ranged cavalry."]},{"title":"Unique Haudenosaunee units","items":["Haudenosaunee War Chief: The leader of your Tribe. Possesses many powerful bonuses and abilities. Explores, fights, builds Town Centers and Trading Posts.","Travois: Builds Native American Buildings.","Aenna: Bowman. Good against infantry.","Tomahawk: Haudenosaunee warrior that hurls tomahawks into battle. Good against cavalry.","Forest Prowler: Stealthy ranged infantry. Good against infantry and in an ambush.","Ram: Siege warrior. Good against buildings.","Mantlet: Tough Haudenosaunee support unit used to shield your army from enemy fire.","Kanya Horseman: Hand cavalry armed with axes. Good against artillery.","Musket Rider: Ranged cavalry. Good against cavalry.","Light Cannon: Light artillery. Good against infantry and artillery."]},{"title":"Unique Haudenosaunee buildings","items":["Longhouse: Haudenosaunee Longhouse. Supports 15 population.","Siege Workshop: Trains and upgrades artillery."]},{"title":"Unique Haudenosaunee ceremonies","items":["Founder Ceremony: Spawns Travois.","Earth Mother Ceremony: Increases population."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/e/e4/Flag_IroquoisDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"hausa","name":"Hausa","page":"Hausa","intro":"The Hausa are an African civilization in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - The African Royals. They are based on the Hausa kingdoms during the 15th to 18th centuries, located between the Niger River and Lake chad, east of Mali, in parts of present-day Nigeria, Niger, Burkina Faso, Benin, Ghana, and Togo.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Africa"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique building"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Kano"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Queen Amina"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with five Villagers, a Livestock Market Builder, a Sanga Cattle with 400 food (which start gathering automatically), and 3 additional Sanga Cattle with 135 food each; all Trading Post sites visible.","Gets a free Sanga Cattle with all shipments, but Home City shipments require +8% xp to be earned.","Can trade livestock in the Livestock Market for wood and coin.","Builds Universities, which provide unique technologies.","Choose Alliances to advance in Age.","Minor civilization units, technologies, and Mercenaries\u0027 costs are replaced by influence. Native warriors and artillery are upgraded automatically for free in every Age up."]},{"title":"Shared African units","items":["Hausa Villager: Villager that constructs buildings and gathers resources.","Levied Spearman: Quick-training, Spearman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Levied Bowman: Quick-training foot archer who loses hitpoints over time, but gains attack speed at lower health.","Levied Gunner: Musketeer who loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Desert Warrior: Hardy javelin warrior equipped with a large shield. The shield grants different armor types when switching combat stances. Good against cavalry.","Desert Archer: Secretive, skilled archer that can hit distant targets as well as shoot fast at short range. Good against infantry.","Desert Raider: Plundering Desert Raider. Good against buildings.","Javelin Rider: Ranged cavalry. Good against hand cavalry, particularly in melee.","Hausa Fishing Canoe: Gathers Food from Fish or Coin from Whales.","Battle Canoe: Battle Canoe. Powerful, agile warship that can also train units.","Cannon Boat: Cannon Boat. Somewhat expensive, but powerful boat good at blasting ships and builders from a distance."]},{"title":"Shared African buildings","items":["Hut: Supports 10 population.","Livestock Market: Livestock Market. Combines Market and Livestock Pen. Can fatten and sell Livestock for wood or gold.","Field: Slow, infinite source of Food or Coin for up to three gatherers. Builds slowly, but is inexpensive.","Port: Builds and upgrades Fishing Boats and warships. Repairs nearby ships.","Watch Tower: Watch Tower that can be used to defend the border.","War Camp: Trains and upgrades African regular units.","Granary: Improves nearby Food gather rates and lures hunt. Builds slowly but for free. Contains hunting and farming upgrades.","Palace: Powerful, defensive building that can also train units."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Emir: Royal Hausa hero with a fealty aura. Explores, fights, builds Palaces, Universities, and Trading Posts. Good against cavalry.","Sanga Cattle: Herd animal. Fattens over time. Fattens faster if tasked on a Livestock Pen, Farm, or Village.","Griot: Griot. Inspiring musician and storyteller who can increase the work rate of buildings and speed of nearby units. Uses instruments to intimidate enemies which slows their attack speed.","Fulani Archer: Foot Archer armed with a short bow for a fast attack. Good against Heavy Infantry and Ranged Cavalry. Can gather Livestock.","Maigadi: Powerful heavy ranged infantry with a deadly hand attack.","Raider: Mobile Hand Cavalry with decent siege damage. Good against light infantry and villagers.","Lifidi Knight: Heavy hand cavalry with a lot of hitpoints.","Xebec: A powerful, agile mercenary warship that fires faster at close range. Inflicts high damage."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["University: Unique Hausa building that can toggle between XP and Influence generation. Trains Griots and researches Alliance technologies. Most effective when near a Town Center, Trading Post, and Palace."]},{"title":"Alliance units and buildings","items":["Akan","Akan Ankobia","Berbers","Berber Nomad","Berber Salt Camel","Berber Camel Rider","British","Arsenal Wagon","Frigate","Fulani","Goat","Hausa","Hausa Builder","Kingdom Builder","Morrocans","Zouave","Mosque","Imam","Muhbir","Yoruba","Yoruba Oyo Legionary","Yoruba Eso Rider"]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/a/aa/Flag_Hausa.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"incaageofempiresiii","name":"Inca","page":"Inca (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Inca are a playable Native American civilization introduced in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition. They are based on the Inca Empire (1438-1572) which ruled over modern-day Peru, Chile, Ecuador, and parts of Bolivia, Argentina, and Colombia.\nThey first appeared as a minor civilization of the same name in Age of Empires III, in update 47581 the minor civilization was renamed to Quechua.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"South America"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Cuzco"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Huayna Capac"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 3 Crates of Food (300 food), 4 Cords of Wood (400 wood), five Villagers, and a Llama; all Trading Post sites visible.","War Chief aura increases the hit points of nearby native warriors.","Receives a free Chasqui with Exploration Age shipments and each Age-up.","Tambos replace Trading Posts, but minor civilization alliances cost 25% more.","Villagers have a lower train limit (90) and can be garrisoned in Tambos.","Kancha Houses produce food (0.6 food/s).","Priestesses and Llamas can work in the Community Plaza and are counted as one and a half units and a quarter of a unit, respectively.","Military units can garrison in Kallankas and Strongholds.","Build the Community Plaza and task Villagers on it to perform powerful ceremonies.","Choose Tribal Council members to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Native American units","items":["Native Villager: Villager that gathers resources.","Warrior: Quick-training Native defender who quickly loses hit points, becoming less effective over time.","Pistolero: A dangerous outlaw with a pistol.","Comanchero: A dangerous outlaw on horseback.","Renegado: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle.","Captured Mortar: Artillery captured and operated by Native Americans. Fires an exploding shell at buildings or ships.","Native Fishing Boat: Gathers food from Fish or coin from Whales."]},{"title":"Shared Native American buildings","items":["Farm: Slow, infinite source of Food. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Community Plaza: Task Villagers on the Community Plaza to perform a poweful ceremony.","War Hut: Trains and upgrades infantry units as well as defends an area with a ranged attack."]},{"title":"Unique Inca units","items":["Inca War Chief: The leader of your Tribe. Possesses many powerful bonuses and abilities. Explores, fights, builds Town Centers, Strongholds and Tambos.","Priestess: Heals injured units and converts enemy units.","Jungle Bowman: Foot Archer with envenomed arrows, which inflict poison damage over time. Good against Heavy Infantry and Light Ranged Cavalry.","Plumed Spearman: Heavy Infantry armed with a feathered spear. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Bolas Warrior: Ranged warrior who hurls bolas for a wide area of effect. The bola slows down enemies. Good against cavalry.","Huaraca: Anti-building ranged infantry. Good against artillery and buildings.","Maceman: Powerful Heavy Hand Infantry which inflicts splash damage with a large bludgeon. Good against buildings, cavalry, and anything within range.","Chasqui: Inca scout with a great deal of utility. Good against Treasure Guardians and can construct various buildings.","Chimu Runner: Fast moving warrior armed with a mace. Can easily disengage from fights. Good against skirmishers and artillery.","Peruvian Dog: Peruvian Hairless Dog. A smart and agile canine that obeys commands.","Chincha Raft: Strong seagoing raft which fires multiple projectiles."]},{"title":"Unique Inca buildings","items":["Kancha House: Inca House that supports 16 population and produces food.","Tambo: Defensive Inca Trading Post that supports 5 population and can shelter civilians who strengthen its attack.","Kallanka: Military building that trains Inca elite infantry and reduces the population cost of garrisoned units.","Stronghold: A powerful military building that can train and garrison all military units to strengthen its attack."]},{"title":"Unique Inca ceremonies","items":["Moon Ceremony: Generates wood.","Supay Ceremony: Spawns Macemen."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/e/e0/Flag_IncanDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"indiansageofempiresiii","name":"Indians","page":"Indians (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Indians are one of three playable civilizations featured in Age of Empires III: The Asian Dynasties. The civilization is primarily based on the Mughal Empire, that was established by the Persianized Muslim conquerors hailing from modern Uzbekistan, that controlled the vast majority of present-day India and surrounding territories such as Pakistan and Afghanistan, known as Hindustanis, led by the illustrious ruler Akbar the Great under whom the empire reached its zenith. They also have access to units, technologies, and cards which hail from other polities such as the Marathas, the Sikhs, the southern regions, as well as the East India Company/British India.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Asia (South)"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Delhi"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Akbar the Great"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 2 Crates of Food (200 food), 4 Cords of Wood (400 wood), 100 export, and six Hindu Villagers.","Receives a Hindu Villager with Home City shipments (except TEAM and INFINITE ones), but Home City shipments require +9% xp to be earned.","Hindu Villagers cost wood instead of food, cannot gather food from livestock which generates XP instead, and gather export as they gather resources.","Gets the Gang Saw and Log Flume technologies for free automatically.","Land villager changes gather yield for tree by 50%.","Build the Consulate to ally with a European civilization and get their units and technologies by spending export.","Build Wonders to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Asian units","items":["Indian Sentry: Quick-training, Pikeman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Indian Irregular: Quick-training, musketeer who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time."]},{"title":"Shared Asian buildings","items":["Rice Paddy: Slow, infinite source of Food or Coin. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Monastery: Trains repentant outlaws and mercenaries. Provides Monk improvements.","Indian Castle: A powerful defensive building that can also train and upgrade artillery.","Consulate: Spend Export here to enter into relations with European powers and gain a powerful bonus. Also use Export to purchase European troops and technologies."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Brahmin: Religious leader and healer with a Stomp area attack that can stun Treasure Guardians. Explores, fights, and builds Town Centers and Trading Posts.","Hindu Villager: An Indian villager that does not eat livestock. Gathers all other resources.","Sacred Cow: Herd animal. Generates experience points. Increased experience points generation when tasked to a Sacred Field.","Rajput: Fast-moving sword gauntlet infantry. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Sepoy: Powerful Indian heavy infantry that has a slight bonus versus cavalry at range and a large bonus versus cavalry at melee.","Gurkha: Nepalese skirmisher that is accurate to a long range. Good against infantry.","Urumi Swordsman: Uses a sword whip that does area damage. Good against heavy infantry. Available only from the Home City.","Sowar: Indian hand cavalry that rides a camel. Good against archers, skirmishers, and artillery.","Zamburak: Ranged camel cavalry. Good against cavalry.","Flail Elephant: Powerful Elephant from India that swings a mace for area damage. Good against buildings.","Mahout Lancer: Heavy hand cavalry that inflicts wide-area damage. Exceptionally deadly against archers and skirmishers.","Howdah: High-hitpoints ranged Elephant cavalry effective against cavalry and artillery.","Siege Elephant: Elephant armed with a cannon. Good against artillery and buildings."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Sacred Field: Livestock generate more experience points when tasked to a Sacred Field. Trains Cows.","Mango Grove: A grove of mango trees that can be harvested for Wood.","Caravanserai: Trains and upgrades hand and ranged cavalry."]},{"title":"Wonders","items":["Agra Fort: Powerful, defensive building that can also train units.","Charminar Gate: Trains mansabdars that increase attack and hitpoints of your troops.","Karni Mata: Increases gather rate of nearby units.","Taj Mahal: Casts the Cease Fire ability to stop combat.","Tower of Victory: Casts the Inspiration ability, which greatly increases the attack, hitpoints, and speed of your land units."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/1/1f/Flag_IndianDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"italiansageofempiresiii","name":"Italians","page":"Italians (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Italians are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - Knights of the Mediterranean.\nThe Italian colonization of the New World was very limited, with the exception of the scrapped Thornton expedition by Ferdinando I de\u0027 Medici, Grand Duke of Tuscany. Despite this, the Italian city-states and mercenaries played a crucial role in slowing the expansion of the Ottoman Empire in the Ottoman-Habsburg wars, which led to the decline of power and influence of the Ottoman Empire. The Italian city-states united as the Kingdom of Italy in the 19th century and established colonies of their own in Africa, which included modern day Eritrea, Somalia, Libya, and Ethiopia.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Architect\nPavisier\nPapal Guard\nSchiavone\nBersagliere\nPapal Zouave\nPapal Lancer\nPapal Bombard\nLeonardo\u0027s Tank\nGalleass"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Basilica\nLombard"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Culverin (Spingarde)\nMortar (Galilean Mortar)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Venice"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Giuseppe Garibaldi"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Argentina\nBarbary States\nBrazil\nUSR"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 6 Crates of Food (600 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), three Settlers, and one Architect.","The Explorer has +0.25 ranged attack bonus damage and +0.5 hand attack bonus damage against treasure guardians and pets.","Gets a free Settler with every technology and may research those at economic buildings in any age, but Home City shipments require +7% xp to be earned.","Can send Basilica units to spawn at any military shipment point.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Culverin (Spingarde), Mortar (Galilean Mortar)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Architect: Unique civilian who can build for free but very slowly. By paying a wood cost, building foundations in progress will have their construction more quickly and allow settlers to work on them.","Pavisier: Unique crossbowman that can change its armor with different stances. In the Defend Mode and Hold Ground stances, The Pavisier gains dual armor, resisting both ranged and hand damage simultaneously.","Papal Guard: Papal hand infantry that protects nearby allies by absorbing some of the inflicted damage. Can hook enemies with his halberd to slow them down. Possesses a powerful charged attack using his halberd.","Schiavone: Specialized Light Infantry that only counters other Light Infantry, but does so very effectively.","Bersagliere: Skirmisher trained to move fast. Sounds a bugle after defeating an enemy to stun foes and boost ally speed.","Papal Zouave: Papal ranged infantry with high hit points that absorbs some of the damage inflicted to nearby allies. Deals high damage but possesses no damage multipliers. Countered by Artillery.","Papal Lancer: Papal heavy cavalry that absorbs some of the damage inflicted to nearby allies. Counters Infantry. Has no negative damage multipliers against Heavy Infantry.","Papal Bombard: Papal Artillery that absorbs some of the damage inflicted to nearby allies. Good against Infantry.","Leonardo\u0027s Tank: Armored vehicle with cannons pointing in all directions. Let\u0027s have a ride on the merry-go-round!","Galleass: Slow, powerful ship resistant to building fire that can train units."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Basilica: Ships powerful Papal allies and boosts nearby building construction speed.","Lombard: Trains Outlaws and Mercenaries, but is also host to a unique investment mechanic, allowing the conversion of resources for free, but over time."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Philosopher Prince, The Medici (Commerce Age)","The Adventurer, The Bishop, The Gentleman Pirate, The Marksman, The Mercenary Contractor (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The Logistician, The Papal Guard, The Pope (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Inventor, The Mercenary Contractor, The Royalist (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Argentina, Barbary States, Brazil, and USR."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/a/ad/Flag_ItalianDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"japaneseageofempiresiii","name":"Japanese","page":"Japanese (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Japanese are one of the three playable civilizations featured in Age of Empires III: The Asian Dynasties. The civilization is based on the Edo period of Japanese history where the Tokugawa Shogunate ruled over most parts of modern Japan.\nTheir precursors in the series are the Yamato in Age of Empires, the Japanese in Age of Empires II, and the Japanese Age of Empires IV.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Asia (East)"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Edo"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Tokugawa Ieyasu"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 3 Cords of Wood (300 wood), 1 Chests of Coin (100 coin), 100 export, six Villagers, and one (two if there are no Berry Bushes near the starting Town Center) Orchard Rickshaw.","Most Home City Cards can be sent twice.","Villagers cannot hunt, have a lower train limit (75), and gather export as they gather resources.","Shrines attract animals to generate resources.","Build the Consulate to ally with a European civilization or enter isolationism and get their units and technologies by spending export.","Build Wonders to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Asian units","items":["Japanese Sentry: Quick-training, Pikeman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Japanese Irregular: Quick-training, musketeer who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time."]},{"title":"Shared Asian buildings","items":["Rice Paddy: Slow, infinite source of Food or Coin. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Monastery: Trains repentant outlaws and mercenaries. Provides Monk improvements.","Japanese Castle: A powerful defensive building that can also train and upgrade artillery.","Consulate: Spend Export here to enter into relations with European powers and gain a powerful bonus. Also use Export to purchase European troops and technologies."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Sohei Archer: Leader who stuns Treasure guardians and has a chance to do Divine Strike damage in combat. Explores, fights, and builds Town Centers, Trading Posts, and Shrines.","Japanese Villager: A Japanese villager that does not eat meat. Gathers all other resources.","Yumi Archer: Ranged infantry armed with the Japanese longbow. Good against infantry.","Ashigaru Musketeer: Japanese heavy foot soldier armed with a musket. Good against cavalry in a melee.","Samurai: Powerful Japanese Samurai swordsman that inflicts area damage in hand combat. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Yamabushi: Japanese Monk armed with a large two-handed club. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Shinobi: Stealthy ranged infantry. Good against infantry.","Naginata Rider: Heavy cavalry armed with a naginata for killing archers, skirmishers, and artillery.","Yabusame Archer: Japanese master of the bow and the horse. Good against cavalry and artillery.","Daimyo: Powerful Japanese lord who can train troops and receive Shipments.","Shogun Tokugawa: Supreme ruler of Japan. Can train troops and receive Shipments. Also gives nearby troops extra hitpoints.","Flaming Arrow: Japanese cannon that shoots an exploding arrow. Better against infantry and artillery than buildings.","Morutaru: Artillery that fires an exploding shell at buildings or ships.","Fune: Fune. Good at exploring, fishing or transport.","Atakebune: Atakebune. Slow, powerful ship resistant to building fire that can train units.","Tekkousen: Tekkousen. Heavy warship."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Shrine: Generates a tiny amount of resources. Configure it to produce different things. Attract nearby animals for bonus production. Supports 10 population.","Cherry Orchard: A beautiful Cherry Orchard which can be harvested for Food.","Dojo: Generates armies automatically. Configure it to produce different things. Can only be sent from the Home City."]},{"title":"Wonders","items":["Golden Pavilion: Increases the attack of ranged land units, the attack of hand units, the speed of all land units, or the hitpoints of all land units. Configure it to give bonuses to different things.","Great Buddha: Casts the Informers spell which reveals the enemy\u0027s positions to you.","The Shogunate: Decreases training time and cost of land military units.","Torii Gates: Increases the experience point build bounty for training units and constructing buildings and the bounty for defeating enemy units and buildings.","Toshogu Shrine: Acts as a giant Shrine and increases the amount of resources that Shrines generate. Supports 20 population."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/4/4e/Flag_JapaneseDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"lakota","name":"Lakota","page":"Lakota","intro":"The Lakota (known as Sioux before the Definitive Edition), are a civilization in Age of Empires III: The WarChiefs, based on one of the three prominent Native American peoples of the Oceti Sakowin (also called Sioux).\nThey first appeared as a minor civilization of the same name in Age of Empires III, and when made playable in The WarChiefs, the minor civilization was replaced by the Cheyenne. They are primarily an aggressive civilization, who lack artillery units, and have limited infantry, but possess various cavalry unit types for different purposes. They have Axe Riders, Tokala Soldiers, heavy infantry and the Charging Ceremony to cover their lack of artillery.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"North American"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Great Council"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Chief Gall"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 1 Cords of Wood (100 wood), 1 Chests of Coin (100 coin), and five Villagers; all Trading Post sites visible.","War Chief aura increases the speed of nearby friendly units.","Begins with 200 population, but cannot build walls until the Industrial Age.","Land villager changes gather yield for huntable animals by 10%.","Cannot gather coin by mining; build a Tribal Marketplace next to a mine and assign Villagers on it to gather coin from the mine instead.","Build the Community Plaza and task Villagers on it to perform powerful ceremonies.","Choose Tribal Council members to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Shared Native American units","items":["Native Villager: Villager that gathers resources.","Lakota Healer: Heals injured units.","Native Scout: A Native American scout. Good for exploration, but has a weak attack.","Warrior: Quick-training Native defender who quickly loses hit points, becoming less effective over time.","Pistolero: A dangerous outlaw with a pistol.","Comanchero: A dangerous outlaw on horseback.","Renegado: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle.","Captured Mortar: Artillery captured and operated by Native Americans. Fires an exploding shell at buildings or ships.","Native Fishing Boat: Gathers food from Fish or coin from Whales.","Canoe: Native boat that can attack or transport units.","War Canoe: Strong in naval combat when built in number."]},{"title":"Shared Native American buildings","items":["Tribal Marketplace: Source of Coin that lasts longer. Must be built next to a Mine. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Farm: Slow, infinite source of Food. Limited to 10 gatherers.","Community Plaza: Task Villagers on the Community Plaza to perform a powerful ceremony.","War Hut: Trains and upgrades infantry units as well as defends an area with a ranged attack.","Corral: Trains and upgrades hand and ranged cavalry."]},{"title":"Unique Lakota units","items":["Lakota War Chief: The leader of your Tribe. Possesses many powerful bonuses and abilities. Explores, fights, builds Town Centers and Trading Posts.","Cetan Bowman: Foot archer. Good against infantry.","Club Warrior: Foot warrior armed with a deadly club. Good against cavalry.","Wakina Rifle: Light infantry with low hitpoints, but a long-ranged attack. Good against infantry.","Axe Rider: Mounted warrior good against skirmishers, foot archers, and artillery.","Bow Rider: Ranged raiding cavalry. Good against cavalry.","Rifle Rider: Ranged cavalry that are effective against cavalry, heavy infantry, and artillery.","Tashunke Prowler: Stealthy horsemen that grow in strength as they grow in number.","Tokala Soldier: Superior lance-carrying horsemen."]},{"title":"Unique Lakota buildings","items":["Teepee: Provides a hitpoint and gathering rate boost to nearby units."]},{"title":"Unique Lakota ceremonies","items":["Charging Ceremony: Increases all units\u0027 siege attack.","Tokala Ceremony: Spawns Tokala Soldiers."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/4/43/Flag_SiouxDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"maltese","name":"Maltese","page":"Maltese","intro":"The Maltese are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - Knights of the Mediterranean, which is based on the Knights Hospitaller of Malta as a vassal state of the Kingdom of Sicily during 1530-1798.\nUnlike the Italians, who are the other civilization added in Knights of the Mediterranean, the Maltese had colonies in the New World between 1651 and 1665, as they bought several islands in the Caribbean as part of an agreement with the French before the islands were sold back to the French West India Company, which brought their colonial project to an end. Much like the Italians, the Knights Hospitaller played a crucial role in slowing the expansion of the Ottoman Empire into Europe, as they manage to hold out on their own in the Great Siege of Malta.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Grand Master\nHospitaller\nSentinel\nFire Thrower\nOrder Galley\nFire Ship"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Hospital\nCommandery\nDepot\nFixed Gun"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Crossbowman (Arbalester)\nCulverin (Basilisk)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Valletta"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Jean Parisot"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Livonia\nBarbary States\nHungary"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), 1 Chests of Coin (100 coin), and six Settlers.","Have the Grand Master instead of Explorer.","Maltese units (except Order units) get +2% hit points (artillery and ships get +1% instead) with each Home City shipment (except infinite ones) and regenerate hit points when idle, but Home City shipments require +1% xp to be earned, and the Maltese will keep the +1% XP requirement even after revolting (Maltese units can still get +2% hit points through Home City shipments of the revolutionary deck, except infinite ones, although it doesn\u0027t affect revolutionary units).","Can train Order units: multinational European soldiers with +10% hit points and attack, +10% XP bounty, and are upgraded automatically, but with increased cost and training time.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Crossbowman (Arbalester), Culverin (Basilisk)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Grand Master: The hero of your civilization. Explores, fights, builds Fortifications and Trading Posts. Cannot die. If he falls unconscious, he can be rescued.","Lamb of the Creator: Intrepid sheep scout that cannot attack. Has high hitpoints, to save others.","Hospitaller: A Knight of Malta armed with a great sword. Absorbs some of the damage inflicted to nearby allies. Faster near Buildings.","Sentinel: Defensive Musketeer that may construct Outposts. Stronger near Buildings, especially Fortifications.","Fire Thrower: Light Infantry that attacks with incendiary weapons which inflict burning damage. Counters Heavy Infantry and Light Cavalry.","Order Galley: Armored, but fast Galley. Good at exploring, fishing and transport. Gains an attack boost after sinking enemy Ships.","Fire Ship: Fire Ship. Rams anything on the water and explodes (only available after sending the Greek Fire card)."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Hospital: Trains Maltese infantry. Heals idle units.","Commandery: Defensive Building. Units that can be garrisoned may be deployed from ANY other Commandery. Trains powerful foreign allies from around Europe who pledge their allegiance to the Knights of St John.","Depot: Depot filled to the brim with gunpowder. Boosts attack speed of nearby Gunpowder Units, Artillery and Buildings. Will EXPLODE if destroyed, damaging ALL units.","Fixed Gun: Powerful stationary artillery."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Adventurer, The Bishop, The Mercenary Contractor, The Sergeant at Arms (Fortress Age)","The Engineer, The Logistician, The Papal Guard, The War Minister, The Pope (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Scottish Marshal (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Barbary States, Hungary, Livonia."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/6/6a/Flag_MalteseDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"mexicans","name":"Mexicans","page":"Mexicans","intro":"The Mexicans are a Federal American civilization introduced as DLC to Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition.\nAnnounced on November 22, 2021 for Steam and the Microsoft Store, it was released on December 1 of the same year.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"North America"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Mexico City"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Miguel Hidalgo"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Baja California or Central America\nRio Grande or Yucatan\nCalifornia or Texas\nMaya (via Yucatán only)"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), 1 Chests of Coin (100 coin), six Settlers, and a Cow.","Settlers have a lower train limit (85).","Receives the Padre in the Commerce Age, who acts as a unique Priest that can pacify enemies.","Choose Federal States to advance in Age and add new Home City Cards to the Deck, starting with fewer cards (21) than other civilizations.","Can revolt in the Commerce, Fortress, and Industrial Ages, and (for some revolutionary nations) revert back to the Mexicans."]},{"title":"National Guard units","items":["Salteador (Vigilante), Chinaco (Charro)."]},{"title":"Shared Federal American units","items":["General MX: The hero of the civilization. Explores, fights, builds Forts and Trading Posts. Cannot die. If he falls unconscious, he can be rescued.","Sloop: Small and nimble warship. Good at exploring, fishing or transport.","Steamer: Powerful, steam-propelled warship resistant to building fire that can train units, construct docks and gather fish.","Ironclad: Advanced armored warship."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Padre: Heroic Mexican Priest. Explores, fights, builds Cathedrals and Trading Posts. Cannot die. If he falls unconscious, he can be rescued.","Insurgente: An insurgent peasant armed with whatever they could find. Good against cavalry and buildings.","Soldado: Very sturdy, but slow training, Heavy Infantry armed with a musket and grenades.","Salteador: Stealthy Skirmisher that can see the location of enemies he recently damaged.","Desperado: A dangerous outlaw with two pistols. Can attack with both pistols at the same time.","Bandido: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle. Throws dynamite to damage infantry or buildings.","Chinaco: Heavy cavalry armed with a lance for extra range. Good against skirmishers, and holds its own against cavalry.","Cuatrero: A dangerous outlaw on horseback. Ranged Cavalry with a Lasso ability."]},{"title":"Revolutionary units","items":["Filibuster: Freewheeling heavy infantry on an unauthorized military expedition. Constructs buildings or destroys them with dynamite.\nRevolting to Baja California turns Settlers into Filibusters.","Californio: Ranged Cavalry with a Lasso ability. Good against cavalry.\nRevolting to California turns Settlers into Californios.","Cruzob Avenger: Cruzob Skirmisher. Salteador with extra speed, range, and Line of Sight. Revolting to Maya turns Salteadores into Cruzob Avengers.","Cruzob Infantry: Cruzob Musketeer that counters cavalry from range.\nRevolting to Maya turns Soldados into Cruzob Infantry.","Revolutionary: Solid general-purpose infantry. Good against cavalry.\nRevolting to Rio Grande turns Settlers into Revolutionaries; Revolting to Central America or Yucatán keep the Settlers, but Town Centers will produce Revolutionaries instead; Central America Revolutionaries have 25% less hit points and damage.","State Militia: Skirmisher with low range that sacrifices attack for hitpoints. Gains additional hitpoints in groups.\nRevolting to Texas turns Settlers into Volunteers and allows them to be trained in place of Settlers and Insurgentes.","Yucateco Insurgente: Veteran Insurgente with 10% more damage and a Lasso ability. Revolting to Yucatan turns Insurgentes into Yucateco Insurgentes. Revolting to Yucatán keeps the Settlers, but they can become Yucateco Insurgentes with the card Plan de Mérida."]},{"title":"Shared Federal American buildings","items":["Saloon: Trains sinister outlaws and mercenaries."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Cathedral: Mexican Church building that can revive a fallen Padre, protects nearby buildings, and has powerful unique upgrades.","Hacienda: Economic building that combines Estate, Mill, and Livestock Pen."]},{"title":"Federal States","items":["Chiapas, Durango, Michoacán, Querétaro, Tlaxcala (Commerce Age)","Coahuila, San Luis Potosí, Sinaloa, Sonora, Tabasco (Fortress Age)","Chihuahua, Guanajuato, Guerrero, Tamaulipas, Zacatecas (Industrial Age)","Estado de México, Jalisco, Oaxaca, Puebla, Veracruz (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Baja California or Central America (Commerce Age).","Rio Grande or Yucatan (Fortress Age).","California or Texas (Industrial Age).","Maya (Yucatán Revolution)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/4/41/Flag_MexicanDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"ottomansageofempiresiii","name":"Ottomans","page":"Ottomans (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Ottomans are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. The Ottoman Empire was a state of Turkish origin which attained the status of great power in Europe in the Early Modern Age (1299–1923 AD). At the peak of their might from the mid sixteenth to the late seventeenth century, they controlled modern day Turkey, the Balkans, parts of the Middle East, and much of the North African coast.\nDespite some interest in it, the Ottomans did not conquer or colonize the New World, although there are some highly disputable claims that they tried to take some minor areas in the Caribbean. The Ottomans were active in Indian Sea and clashed with the Portuguese in Africa, India, and Southeast Asia, but never achieved its status as a global maritime power due to constant challenges from other Western civilizations and its geographical location. The only colony-like possession that they held was Egypt.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Africa (North)\nAsia (Caucasus, Middle East)\nEurope (Caucasus, Balkans)"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Town Centers automatically trains Yörüks\nYörük production can be increased at the Mosque"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Yoruk\nImam\nBashibozuk\nJanissary\nAzap\nAbus Gunner\nHumbaraci\nMuhbir\nNizam Fusilier\nDeli\nSipahi\nGreat Bombard\nGalley"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Mosque"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Deli (Rumeliot)\nHumbaraci (Ulufeli)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Istanbul"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Suleiman the Magnificent"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Barbary States\nEgypt\nHungary\nRomania"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 1 Crates of Food (100 food), 3 Cords of Wood and 1 Tiny Crate of Wood (350 wood), and six Yörüks.","The Explorer has +5% hit points.","Town Centers automatically spawn Yörüks, with the rate that can be increased by improvements at the Mosque.","Yörüks have a low limit (25) which can be increased by improvements at the Mosque, and build Town Centers 50% slower.","Artillery have +2 Line of Sight ([[Culverin (Age of Empires III).","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Deli (Rumeliot), Humbaraci (Ulufeli)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Yoruk: Ottoman villager that arrives for free at the Town Center.","Imam: Heals injured units.","Bashibozuk: Quick-training, infantryman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","Janissary: Powerful Ottoman infantry that acts like a powerful Musketeer.","Azap: Heavy infantry. Good against cavalry. Armed with a bow to counter light cavalry at range.","Abus Gunner: Ottoman infantry that inflicts siege damage. Good against infantry.","Humbaraci: Heavy grenade-thrower infantryman that is effective against buildings and artillery, but more vulnerable to infantry and cavalry.","Muhbir: Sneaky assassin. Highly effective against mercenaries and heroes such as Explorers. Attacks faster with less hitpoints and benefits from promotions.","Nizam Fusilier: Exceptionally well-drilled ranged infantry that specializes in utilizing the advantages of different formations. (Definitive Edition onwards)","Deli: Ottoman hand cavalry with increased movement and attack speed.","Sipahi: Powerful cavalry available only from the Home City.","Great Bombard: Ottoman super-heavy artillery. Moves and fires slowly, but does tremendous damage against infantry, ships and buildings.","Galley: Galley. Good at exploring, fishing or transport."]},{"title":"Unique building","items":["Mosque: Trains healers and provides colony improvements and unique improvements."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Imam, The Inventor, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Exiled Prince, The Marksman, The Mercenary Contractor, The Scout (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The Grand Vizier, The Logistician, The Tycoon (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Inventor, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Bernardo O\u0027Higgins and Francisco de Paula Santander (in The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Barbary States, Egypt (exclusive), Hungary, and Romania (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/a/a1/Flag_OttomanDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"polesageofempiresiii","name":"Poles","page":"Poles (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Poles are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition - The Baltic Powers. They represent the . As such, they are the successors to the Poles and Lithuanians from Age of Empires II.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Hetman\nPiechur\nRetainer\nWinged Hussar"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Folwark\nSejm"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Warsaw"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Jan Sobieski"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Fortress Age:\nCossack Hetmanate\nLivonia\nIndustrial Age: Duchy of Warsaw\nHungary\nUnited States"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), and six Settlers.","Buildings (except walls) cost 15% less wood and have 15% less build time, but have -18% hit points (except Town Centers and walls).","Start with a Hetman, a cavalry hero who can contruct the Sejm, a building that produces the chosen resource based on Settler population, and replaces the Capitol.","Folwarks replace Mills and Livestock Pens, and can be individually upgraded."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Pikeman (Scytheman), Piechur (Kurpie Marksman), Retainer (Vanguard), Cavalry Archer (Pancerny)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Hetman: Hetman. The hero of your civilization. Explores, fights, builds the Sejm, Town Centers, and Trading Posts. Cannot die. If he falls unconscious, he can be rescued.","Piechur: Versatile Rifleman. Good against all infantry.","Retainer: Quick, Affordable Hand Cavalry. Good against other Cavalry.","Winged Hussar: Fast heavy Polish elite cavalryman with extra attack range and a powerful Winged lance charge."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Folwark: Infinite food source that supports 10 population and can train basic soldiers. Can be upgraded with specializations.","Sejm: Powerful economic building that can produce resources based on Settler count and improve their gather rates."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["Commerce Age: The Governor, The Philosopher Prince, The Inventor, The Naturalist, The Logistician","Fortress Age: The Gentleman Pirate, The Exiled Prince, The Mercenary Contractor, The Marksman, The Scout","Industrial Age: The Tycoon, The Logistician, The Pope, The Viceroy, The Cavalry Marshal","Imperial Age: El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Fortress Age: Cossack Hetmanate, Livonia","Industrial Age: Duchy of Warsaw, Hungary, United States"]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/7/7e/AoE3DE_Flag_Poles.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"portugueseageofempiresiii","name":"Portuguese","page":"Portuguese (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Portuguese are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. The Portuguese Empire was a global empire which grew wealthy from their control of trade routes connecting Portugal through Africa, Middle East, India, Southeast Asia, and Japan, and established trading posts and colonies with significant ones being in South America and Africa. In the New World, the Portuguese controlled a large amount of land in the eastern parts of South America until 1822 (most notably Brazil).\nThe Portuguese also appear in Age of Empires II HD: The African Kingdoms.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"European"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Free Covered Wagon with every Age advance"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Cassador\nOrdinance Rifleman\nOrgan Gun"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Crossbowman (Order Besteiro)\nOrdinance Rifleman\nPikeman (Ordinance Pikeman)\nMusketeer (Legionario)\nDragoon (Legion Dragoon)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Lisbon"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Henry the Navigator"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Barbary States\nBrazil\nGran Colombia\nIndonesia\nPeru"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 2 Crates of Food, 1 Tiny Crates of Food (250 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), and seven Settlers.","The Explorer has the Spyglass ability.","Receives a free Covered Wagon with every Age.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Crossbowman (Age of Empires III), [[Ordinance Rifleman (Ordinance Rifleman), Pikeman (Age of Empires III), [[Musketeer (Legionario), Dragoon (Legion Dragoon)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Cassador: Skirmisher with low hit points, but a strong attack. Good against infantry.","Ordinance Rifleman: Skirmisher good against infantry.","Organ Gun: Artillery that fires multiple projectiles. Better against infantry than buildings."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Ethiopian Queen, The Exiled Prince, The Marksman, The Mercenary Contractor (Fortress Age)","The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Papal Guard, The Tycoon, The Viceroy (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Inventor, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Miguel Hidalgo and José Bonifácio de Andrada e Silva (until the The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Barbary States, Brazil, Gran Colombia, Indonesia, and Peru (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/7/7d/Flag_PortugueseDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"russians","name":"Russians","page":"Russians","intro":"The Russians are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. They are based on the Russian Empire, which lasted from 1721 until the modern era, and controlled significant sections of northeastern Europe and northern Asia.\nIn the New World (Americas), the Russians took little land, but they did occupy Alaska. They placed trading posts in Alaska, the Aleutian Islands, British Columbia, Washington, Oregon, Hawaii, and as far south as Fort Ross in northern California, some 50 miles north of San Francisco.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe\nAsia"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Train Settlers and infantry in groups\nBlockhouses act as both a Barracks and an Outpost"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Strelet\nRekrut\nPoruchik\nCossack\nOprichnik"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Blockhouse"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Cavalry Archer (Dvoryanin)\nGrenadier (Pavlov Grenadier)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"St. Petersburg"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Ivan the Terrible"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Finland\nHungary\nRomania"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 5 Crates of Food (500 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), and five Settlers.","The Explorer has +3 siege attack damage.","Has a population limit of 210.","Settlers and Blockhouse infantry are trained in groups; Blockhouse infantry units cost -25% and have -25% train time, but -20% hit points and damage; Settlers cost -13% and have +108% train time (reducing total training time -30% in batches of 3).","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Cavalry Archer (Dvoryanin), Grenadier (Pavlov Grenadier)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Strelet: Weak but cheap skirmisher. Good against infantry.","Rekrut: Affordable Russian musketeer. Armed with a bayonet to beat cavalry.","Poruchik: Russian junior officer. Heavy hand infantry with a large attack.","Cossack: Russian hand cavalry.","Oprichnik: Hand cavalry good at raiding villagers or buildings."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Blockhouse: Russian combination of Barracks and Outpost. Can defend the frontier or train infantry in groups. Also provides 5 population."]},{"title":"Allies, mercenaries and natives","items":["Mercenaries shippable from the Home City: Jaeger, Black Rider, Landsknetchs, Swiss Pikeman, Highlander, Harquebusier, Manchu, Pandour, Giant Grenadier, Li\u0027l Bombard, Privateer.","Native warriors shippable from the Home City: Royal Arquebusier, Boyar, Nootka Clubman, Royal Huntsman."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince, The Quartermaster (Commerce Age)","The Adventurer, The Bishop, The Exiled Prince, The Gentleman Pirate, The Scout (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Logistician, The War Minister (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Simón Bolívar and Francisco de Paula Santander (since the The WarChiefs).","Finland, Hungary, and Romania (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/b/b3/Flag_RussianDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"spanishageofempiresiii","name":"Spanish","page":"Spanish (Age of Empires III)","intro":"The Spanish are a playable European civilization in Age of Empires III. They are based on the Spanish Empire which started with the union of the crowns of Castille and Aragon and their consolidation of Spain in 1492.\nThe Spanish are a European Catholic nation that was the first European country to successfully colonise the Americas and create a world empire. They are well known for having defeated and annexed the majority of Native American civilizations, especially the Aztecs and Maya in Mesoamerica, and the Inca in South America. From the wealth of an immeasurable amount of precious metals (primarily gold and silver) from American mines, they also waged several wars with religious motivations against non-Catholic countries such as the Netherlands, England, and the Ottoman Empire.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Earn Home City shipments faster"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"War Dog\nMissionary\nRodelero\nLancer"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Pikeman (Tercio)\nRodelero (Espadachin)\nLancer (Garrochista)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Seville"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Queen Isabella"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Argentina\nChile\nGran Colombia\nMexico\nPeru"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 3 Crates of Food (300 food), 2 Cords of Wood (200 wood), six Settlers, and a War Dog.","The Explorer can train War Dogs.","Home City shipments require -25% xp to be earned.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Pikeman (Tercio), Rodelero (Espadachin), Lancer (Garrochista)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["War Dog: War Dog. A fierce canine that obeys commands.","Missionary: Unique Spanish healer with a speedy mount. Doesn’t cost population.","Rodelero: Fast-moving sword and buckler infantry.","Lancer: Heavy cavalry armed with a lance for killing infantry."]},{"title":"Allies, mercenaries and natives","items":["Mercenaries shippable from the Home City: Irish Brigadier, Highlander, Armored Pistoleer, Elmetto, Swiss Pikeman, Fusilier, Mediterranean Army, Highland Army, Holy Roman Army.","Natives shippable from the Home City: Maya Holcan Javelineer, Mounted Infantry, Royal Musketeer."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince (Commerce Age)","The Admiral of the Ocean Sea, The Adventurer, The Bishop, The Scout, The Sergeant at Arms (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Papal Guard, The War Minister (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Inventor, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Miguel Hidalgo and Bernardo O\u0027Higgins (The WarChiefs and The Asian Dynasties).","Argentina, Chile (exclusive), Gran Colombia, Mexico (exclusive), and Peru (since the Definitive Edition)."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/4/4d/Flag_SpanishDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"swedes","name":"Swedes","page":"Swedes","intro":"The Swedes are one of the two civilizations introduced in Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition, the other being the Inca. They are descendants of the Vikings who inhabited Scandinavia, and are based on the Swedish Empire which began under the reign of Gustavus Adolphus in 1611.\nIn comparison with the other European states, Swedish colonization in the Americas was quite minor: the Swedes held the Delaware River (then called \"New Sweden\") from 1638 to 1655, Saint-Barthélemy from 1784 to 1878, and Guadeloupe from 1813 to 1814, and are more famous for their migration to Minnesota in the 19th century.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"Europe"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"Torps gather adjacent resources\nCheaper and faster mercenary shipments\nAdvanced Arsenal technologies available"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"Carolean\nHakkapelit\nLeather Cannon"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"Torp"},{"label":"Muhafız birlikleri","key":"Royal","value":"Pikeman (Dalkarl)\nHakkapelit (Drabant)"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Stockholm"},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"Gustavus Adolphus"},{"label":"Devrimler","key":"Revolution","value":"Livonia\nFinland\nUSR"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 1 Crates of Food, 1 Tiny Crate of Food (150 food), 3 Cords of Wood (300 wood), and six Settlers.","The Explorer has +1 hand attack damage.","Settlers have a lower train limit (90).","Torps gather nearby resources.","Jaegers and Black Riders can always be recruited from the Tavern.","Mercenary shipments are cheaper (-10% coin) and arrive quickly (-20 seconds).","Advanced improvements available at the Arsenal.","Choose Politicians to advance in Age."]},{"title":"Royal Guard units","items":["Pikeman (Dalkarl), Hakkapelit (Drabant)."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Carolean: Swedish Musketeer that fires quickly and counters cavalry from range. Can charge quickly with his sword equipped. Good in melee combat.","Hakkapelit: Light ranged cavalry from Finland with a powerful hand attack as well as a short-ranged attack inflicting area damage.","Leather Cannon: Light affordable artillery that can fire and reposition quickly. Good against infantry."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Torp: Swedish House that supports 10 population and gathers nearby resources. Spawns a small Berry Bush."]},{"title":"Politicians","items":["The Governor, The Inventor, The Logistician, The Naturalist, The Philosopher Prince (Commerce Age)","The Bishop, The Exiled Prince, The Gentleman Pirate, The Marksman, The Mercenary Contractor (Fortress Age)","The Cavalry Marshal, The Engineer, The King\u0027s Musketeer, The Papal Guard, The Logistician (Industrial Age)","El Presidente, The General, The Mercenary Contractor, The Knight, The Royalist (Imperial Age)"]},{"title":"Revolutions","items":["Finland, Livonia, USR."]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/7/76/Flag_SwedishDE.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"},{"id":"unitedstates","name":"United States","page":"United States","intro":"The United States of America, simply known as the United States (U.S.), is a Federal American civilization introduced as DLC to Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition.\nPlayer access to the United States can be purchased on Steam or the Xbox App. It could previously be unlocked for free by completing limited-time challenges based on the present-day fifty American states. Since August 13, 2026, the civilization is part of the base game.","info":[{"label":"Kıta","key":"Continent","value":"North America"},{"label":"Özellikler","key":"Features","value":"See Features"},{"label":"Özel birlikler","key":"Unit","value":"See Unique units"},{"label":"Özel bina","key":"Building","value":"See Unique buildings"},{"label":"Ana şehir","key":"HomeCity","value":"Washington D.C."},{"label":"Lider","key":"Personality","value":"George Washington"}],"sections":[{"title":"Civilization bonuses","items":["Starts with 4 Crates of Food (400 food), 2 Cords of Wood (100 wood), 1 Collection of Books (100 xp), and six Settlers.","Settlers have a lower train limit (90).","Has the General as the hero unit, which can plant Inspiring Flags to augment nearby units and buildings, and build Forts instead of Town Centers.","Levy/Conscription can be used repeatedly but with a long global cooldown between each use.","Have access to Immigrant and Legion Home City Cards.","\"Robber Barons\" and \"Industrial Revolution\" are automatically added to the deck in the Industrial Age.","Choose Federal States to advance in Age and add new Home City cards to the Deck, starting with fewer cards (21) than other civilizations.","Federal States grants 200 XP in the Commerce Age, 300 XP in the Fortress Age, 400 XP in the Industrial Age, and 500 XP in the Imperial Age."]},{"title":"National Guard units","items":["State Militia (Volunteer)."]},{"title":"Shared Federal American units","items":["General US: The hero of your civilization. Explores, fights, builds Forts and Trading Posts. Cannot die. If he falls unconscious, he can be rescued.","Sloop: Small and nimble warship. Good at exploring, fishing or transport.","Steamer: Powerful, steam-propelled warship resistant to building fire that can train units, construct docks and gather fish.","Ironclad: Advanced armored warship."]},{"title":"Unique units","items":["Minuteman: Quick-training, Minuteman who quickly loses hitpoints, becoming less effective over time.","State Militia: Skirmisher with low range that sacrifices attack for hitpoints. Gains additional hitpoints in groups.","Regular: Heavy ranged infantry with greater range than other Musketeers. Armed with a bayonet to beat cavalry.","Gunslinger: A dangerous outlaw with a pistol. Can quickly fire 3 shots.","Owlhoot: A dangerous outlaw with a rifle. Can deal AoE damage in a cone in front of him.","Sharpshooter: Skirmisher with a long-ranged attack, but low hitpoints. Gains extra range per upgrade. Good against infantry.","Cowboy: A dangerous outlaw on horseback. Has a high powered shot.","Carbine Cavalry: Ranged light cavalry equipped with a carbine repeater. Good against Heavy Cavalry and Artillery.","Gatling Gun: Early automatic-fire weapon. Better against infantry than buildings.","Quaker Gun: Decoy unit which deals no damage but can take the shape of any common artillery. Good to distract the enemy and to attract enemy fire."]},{"title":"Shared Federal American buildings","items":["Saloon: Trains sinister outlaws and mercenaries."]},{"title":"Unique buildings","items":["Meeting House: Trains healers, provides town improvements and trickles XP.","State Capitol: Wagon training and powerful improvements for your civilization."]},{"title":"Federal States","items":["Delaware, Massachusetts, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Virginia (Commerce Age)","Indiana, Kentucky, Maryland, New Hampshire, Tennessee (Fortress Age)","California, New Jersey, Ohio, South Carolina, Vermont (Industrial Age)","Connecticut, Florida, Illinois, New York, Texas (Imperial Age)"]}],"image":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ageofempires/images/8/8c/Flag_American_act3_aoe3de.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300"}]};
